 36SI c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2015St14:                          
 36SI c  Eur Phys J  A 51, 117 (2015)                                           
 36SI c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL/MSU), November 30, 2015                      
 36SI c  2015St14: Al ions were produced by fragmentation of a 345              
 36SI2c  MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca beam from the RIBF facility at RIKEN on a          
 36SI3c  15 mm beryllium target. Fragments were separated and identified        
 36SI4c  using the BigRIPS spectrometer and the zero-degree spectrometer (ZDS), 
 36SI5c  with energy loss measured by a multi-sampling ionization chamber       
 36SI6c  (MUSIC) and positions by PPACs. The selected ions were implanted into  
 36SI7c  the CAITEN detector (Cylindrical Active Implantation Target for Exotic 
 36SI8c  Nuclei), consisting of a segmented movable hollow-cylindrical-shape    
 36SI9c  plastic scintillator and a stationary ring of 24 position-sensitive    
 36SIac  photomultiplier tubes (PSPMTs). |g rays were detected by three HPGe    
 36SIbc  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, implantation-decay-correlation,          
 36SIcc  |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin, |b|g(t). Deduced levels, J, |p, half-life.       
 36SIdc  Comparison with shell-model calculations.                              
